{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 137, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a direct input-to-output residual where none existed helps much more than swapping out an existing op on that edge (experiments 14, 18, 21, 24 vs 13, 15, 16)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 4 is already missing, removing edge 5 leaves edge 3 as the output's only input, which starves the cell (experiments 3, 6, 9 vs 1, 5)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "A skip into the output is largely redundant when edge 3 already gives an input-to-output skip, so the gain shrinks (experiments 86, 92 vs 85, 91)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the input-to-output residual with a convolution removes the cell's main identity path and tends to hurt trainability (experiment 78)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping out a learnable 1x1 conv on edge 3 loses capacity, unlike filling an empty edge (experiment 15 vs 14, 21)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with parameter-free pooling cuts capacity, while placing pooling on an empty or weaker edge does not (experiment 57 vs 58, 65)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a pooling edge to a 3x3 conv adds the most capacity, compared with replacing skip or 1x1 ops (experiment 41 vs 39, 45)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning a pooling edge into the output into a conv improves feature quality more than replacing skip or 1x1 ops (experiments 31, 33, 36 vs 26, 27)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 2 gets no direct input from node 0, a skip from node 1 keeps information flowing through node 2 (experiment 72 vs 67)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a missing node1-to-node2 connection adds a path, whereas replacing an existing conv only removes capacity (experiments 68, 72 vs 67, 70)."}], "tok": 18172, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_c